course: dictionary
lesson: 12977
title: Strong words of urging
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An exhortation is a strong, serious request that urges people to do something. The word names the urging itself. «The coach's exhortation to the team was simple: never give up.» The coach is pushing the whole team to keep going, and the word exhortation names that push.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Strong and serious tell you it is more than a polite suggestion. «The general gave an exhortation to his soldiers before the battle.» Before a battle, the speech is meant to make people brave and determined, so an exhortation is a powerful speech, not a quiet hint.
explain: The word also has a church meaning. «In church, the minister gave a short exhortation before the prayers.» Here an exhortation is a short talk that encourages people to live well or to get ready for prayer. Use the clues in the sentence to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Exhortation is a noun. Its plural is exhortations.
fact: «Exhortation» means a strong, serious request or speech that urges people to do something.
fact: In church, «exhortation» means a short talk that encourages people to live well or to prepare for prayer or communion.
fact: «Despite all exhortations» means even though people kept urging, so the urging did not work.
fact: Exhortation is a formal word. You will find it in formal writing, history and religion.
exercise: «The general gave an exhortation to his troops before the battle.» What is an exhortation? | A map showing where the battle will be | A list of the soldiers' names | A quiet song sung at night | *A strong, serious speech urging people to act
exercise: «Despite all exhortations from her parents, Maya would not tidy her room.» What does this suggest? | *Her parents kept urging her, but she did not listen | Her parents gave her a prize for tidying | Her parents forgot to speak to her | Maya tidied her room straight away
exercise: In church, what is a short exhortation? | A loud hymn sung by the choir | *A short talk encouraging people to live well or prepare for prayer | A prayer book with pictures in it | A collection of coins for the roof
test: «The coach's exhortation to the team was simple: never give up.» What did the exhortation tell the team to do? | Eat more cake before the match | Stop playing and sit down | *Keep trying and never give up | Go home early
test: Which is the correct plural of exhortation? | *exhortations | exhortating | exhortates | exhortation's
exam: «The minister's exhortation before prayer was short, but it encouraged everyone to live well.» What does exhortation mean here? | A school bell ringing for lunch | *A short talk encouraging people to live well | A quiet walk in the garden | A long song with no words
